Provenance of the Master System and Game Gear machine layer (runtime/guests/sms)

Device behavior is ported from ares, https://github.com/ares-emulator/ares,
commit 0b928930af4cc59ed99e942996f0d3c815379388, ISC license (text below).
The code here is new C11 in relift's catch-up shape; each ported file keeps
the ISC notice in its header.

psg.c     the SN76489 (tone and noise channels, the 16-bit shift register,
          the latch), the console's mix and the Game Gear stereo port
                                   component/audio/sn76489/sn76489.cpp,
                                   ms/psg/psg.cpp
vdp.c     the VDP: ports, registers, VRAM and CRAM, the counters, the line
          and frame interrupts, mode 4 and the TMS9918 graphics modes 1 and
          2, sprites, the colour output
                                   ms/vdp/vdp.cpp, io.cpp, irq.cpp,
                                   background.cpp, sprite.cpp, dac.cpp
sms.c     the machine: memory map, the Sega, Codemasters and Korean
          mappers, the memory control port, the I/O ports, the gamepad and
          the Game Gear's ports and start button, and the clock steps that
          place VDP work on the CPU's timeline
                                   ms/cpu/memory.cpp, ms/cpu/cpu.cpp,
                                   ms/cartridge/board/sega.cpp,
                                   codemasters.cpp, korea.cpp,
                                   ms/controller/gamepad/gamepad.cpp,
                                   ms/system/controls.cpp,
                                   ares/scheduler/thread.cpp
tms9918.c the TMS9918A of the SG-1000: ports, registers, the frame
          interrupt, graphics 1 and 2, text and multicolor modes, sprites,
          the palette
                                   component/video/tms9918/tms9918.cpp,
                                   io.cpp, background.cpp, sprite.cpp,
                                   dac.cpp, sg/vdp/color.cpp
ym2413.c  the YM2413 (OPLL): operators, envelopes, the LFOs, rhythm mode,
          the register writes; the sine and exponent tables precomputed
                                   component/audio/ym2413/ym2413.cpp,
                                   io.cpp, operator.cpp, voice.cpp,
                                   constants.cpp

